WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.792
The heart-rate scenario shows why quality work requires judgment.

00:00:03.792 --> 00:00:07.772
Minus one is clearly incompatible with a normal heart-rate measurement.

00:00:07.772 --> 00:00:10.422
A blank value is a completeness problem.

00:00:10.422 --> 00:00:15.672
Two hundred is unusual, but it may be physiologically possible in some circumstances.

00:00:15.672 --> 00:00:19.097
That means we investigate rather than automatically delete it.

00:00:19.097 --> 00:00:22.857
Quality rules help us identify records that deserve attention.

00:00:22.857 --> 00:00:25.117
They do not replace domain reasoning.

00:00:25.117 --> 00:00:28.657
In practice, quality rules should be tied to a use case.

00:00:28.657 --> 00:00:34.562
A fifteen-minute delay may be acceptable for a monthly report but unacceptable for a real-time alert.

00:00:34.562 --> 00:00:41.572
Likewise, an unusual physiological value should often be flagged and investigated rather than automatically

00:00:41.572 --> 00:00:44.720
deleted. Good cleaning preserves evidence and documents uncertainty.
